{"BlockedEmail.should_block?(email) reads match_count, increments it in Ruby, then saves \u2014 if two requests race, one increment is lost because both read the same value before either saves. Should use increment!(:match_count) for atomic SQL update instead.": 0.9007198214530945, "The regex @(#{domains}) lacks an end-of-string anchor, so user@allowed.com.malicious.org passes whitelist validation when only allowed.com is whitelisted. The pattern matches @allowed.com as a substring anywhere in the domain. Need to add \\z to anchor to the end of the email address.": 0.6670665740966797}